			<Section>
				<Header>Shasta Lake Outflow Temperature, Flow, Elevation, and Gates</Header>

				<Object>
					<Type>textbox</Type>
					<Text>This composite figure includes all aspects of Shasta Dam outflow in four panels. 

The uppermost panel illustrates simulated dam outflow  temperature throughout the calendar year. Time (date) is represented on the x-axis and temperature (%%degrees%%F) is represented on the y-axis. 

The second panel includes flow (cfs) through each modeled gate level and side gate structure through time. Time (date) is represented on the x-axis and temperature (%%degrees%%F) is represented on the y-axis.  These figures show the gate progression through the spring, summer and fall to manage water temperature releases to meet downstream objectives. 

The third panel includes the historical gate use and side gate structure through time. Time (date) is represented on the x-axis and elevation (by TCD gate) is represented on the y-axis.  Each gate level is represented as 5 horizontal bars - where each bar represents one of the 5 gates. These figures show the gate progression through the spring, summer and fall to manage water temperature releases to meet downstream objectives.

The fourth panel includes a plot of simulated and observed Shasta Lake surface elevation (ft) through time, showing the general increase in storage in the spring and then declining elevations through summer and fall. The vertical extent of TCD Gate levels is shown on this panel. 

A table of legend entries and abbreviations follows the figure describing the lines and symbols in the figure.</Text>
				</Object>
